.TH CHTTP_DEFAULT_CLIENT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_default_client \- return the process-level default HTTP client
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

chttpcli chttp_default_client(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the lazily-initialised process-level default client.  Thread-
safe; only one client is ever created per process.

The default client uses default settings (pool_size = CPU count, no
timeouts, TLS verification enabled).  It can be configured via the
same chttpclient_set_* functions as any other client.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Default client handle, or CHTTPCLI_INVALID if initialisation failed.
.fi
.SH WARNINGS
.nf
Do not pass the returned handle to chttpclient_destroy: it is owned
by this module, which destroys it automatically at process exit.
Destroying it yourself will not crash that specific call (the handle
is recognised and this module's own reference to it is cleared), but
the default client is never rebuilt afterward, so every later
chttp_default_client/chttp_do/chttp_get/... call in the process then
fails cleanly instead of performing a request, for the remainder of
that process. If you need a client with a lifetime you control,
create your own via create_chttpclient/create_chttpclient_mp instead.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR create_chttpclient (3),
.BR chttpclient_destroy (3),
.BR chttp_do (3),
.BR chttp_get (3)
